# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the QuranCodex Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version resolved by npm)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Changes
Modified: `next/src/app/_shell.jsx`
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the `<body>` tag, positioned right after the existing `<Analytics />` component

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was added to the Shell component, which serves as the root layout wrapper for both the main application (`app/[locale]/layout.js`) and the admin section (`app/admin/layout.js`). This ensures Speed Insights tracking is enabled across the entire application.

### Why This Location?
- The `_shell.jsx` file contains the shared `<html>` and `<body>` structure used by multiple root layouts
- Placing SpeedInsights here (alongside the existing Analytics component) ensures consistent tracking across all routes
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices for framework-level integrations

### Framework-Specific Implementation
Following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+:
- Used the Next.js-specific import: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Placed the component at the root level in the `<body>` tag
- No additional configuration required - the component works out of the box

